report:
{
 "summary": "In value_chain (more_itertools/more.py), moved the try/except so it only guards getting the iterator: values are checked with iter(value) inside the try (a TypeError there means the value isn't iterable and it is yielded unchanged, as documented), while yield from iterator runs outside the try, so a TypeError raised mid-iteration (e.g. from a lazy map or generator) now propagates to the caller instead of yielding the half-consumed iterator as an item."
}

{
 "summary": "Fixed OrderedMultiDict.addlist (boltons/dictutils.py) and its inline copy used by QueryParamDict (boltons/urlutils.py): the old code tested the truthiness of the raw iterable and iterated it twice (once for the linked list, once for the values list), so one-shot iterators like generators were exhausted before extend() \u2014 leaving getlist()/get() out of sync with repr() \u2014 and an empty generator created an empty-list entry (len 1, keys() empty). addlist now materializes any non-list iterable exactly once (before any truth test, so ambiguous truth values like numpy arrays no longer raise) and returns early when the result is empty, making a one-shot iterable behave exactly like the equivalent list."
}

