{
 "summary": "Fixed the bucket class to track keys that were actually produced by input items in a separate _seen_keys set, avoiding defaultdict creating empty entries that fake keys. The _get_values method now: (1) tracks whether a key was ever seen in _seen_keys, (2) uses try/finally to remove empty cache entries for keys that were never produced by any item, and (3) __iter__ returns _seen_keys instead of _cache. This ensures probing a missing key (via 'in' or []) doesn't make it appear when iterating, while preserving keys that were drained from the cache."
}

{
 "summary": "In more_itertools/more.py, bucket.__init__ replaced the supplied validator with an always-true default whenever it was falsey ('validator or (lambda x: True)'), so a falsey-but-callable validator (e.g. an empty callable set allow-list) was silently ignored by __getitem__, __contains__, and __iter__. Changed the check to 'validator is None' so only an omitted validator falls back to the default; a passed validator is always used, making rejected buckets empty, 'in' return False, key iteration skip them, and rejected keys on infinite sources return immediately."
}

