 "summary": "Fix naturalsize unit carry-over at rounding boundaries in src/humanize/filesize.py: after computing the exponent, (1) walk exp back down when math.log rounds up to an exact integer (e.g. 10**15-1 -> log==5.0, which made truncating formats like %d print '0 PB'), and (2) format the number first and, if its displayed value rounds up to the base (parsed via a leading-number regex so formats with literal text still work), increment exp and re-render so the unit moves with the rounded number (999960 -> '1.0 MB', 1024**3-1 binary -> '1.0 GiB', gnu boundaries too), while guarding exp < len(suffix) so the largest units (QB/QiB) stay put for huge values."
}

